Z||000000||BV MotorSports||06-13-2001||10:12 PM||||Hey all. Just went to a local race and had a minor problem. <BR>For those of you into road racing have you ever had the following happen?<P>During a high speed banked left turn my car just flat out cut out. It was like I ran out of fuel. Fuel guage showed 1 mark below full.<BR>Didnt stumble or back fire...it just bogged down for approx 5 seconds. <BR>First time the car showed 1/2 full...put 4 gallons of gas in it, made another run, no problem. Second run (showing 1 mark below full) then it happend for the second time.<BR>Its just a 1/4 mile track so I doubt I burned off that much fuel between runs.<BR>Ideas???<P>Steven<P><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||5
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||06-13-2001||10:20 PM||||Did you check the oil?? if you run low oil you can trip the pressure sensor , thus shutting down the motor (won't happen with stock suspension) I pulled my pan and had baffels welded into it to keep the oil from sloshing around and getting dry conditions. I had the same thing happen as you did my first year running.<P>Always run a Fiero with a full tank , weight in the center of the car is a must for steady state cornering like on a track.<P>Not sure what gas tank mods can be made if your problem is fuel starvation<P><BR>Baffels in the tank<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||06-13-2001||10:29 PM||||I had the same thing happen to me, although under different circumstances, around I sharp right 90* corner at an autocross about a month ago.  I would run the car deep into the corner, brake hard, turn right, and get back in it (I have a hard time downshifting into 1st, so I did the whole corner in 2nd).  The bogging happened as soon as I planted my right foot, and I couldn't have been turning more than 2000rpm in that gear.<P>Oh, but I did have a backfire.<p>[This message has been edited by Eric (edited 06-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||06-13-2001||10:35 PM||||Your problem is simple .....<P> Due to the lack of a decent baffle system for the oil pan it is very easy to loose oil pressure from the oil moving to one side of the pan during a hard turn, mainly a left turn. When the pump is exposed it is not drawing oil thus no oil pressure. Because the oil pressure switch is wired into the fuel pump system ( three wired connector at switch, one is ground, one is a lead to pressure gauge, third is a lead to the fuel pump relay located next to the A/C relay just behind the driver in the engine compartment).<P> Your solution for this is to have a reputable shop design you a baffle system for your oil pan or send it out to us and we can design and fabricate a system that will solve your problems.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000004||BV MotorSports||06-13-2001||11:02 PM||||Thanks for the quick replys guys. I didnt think it was fuel since I have autoX'ed the car with less then 1/4 showing on the fuel guage.<BR>I need to get this sorted out cause I am going back out wensday night to BEAT the hell out of the "other guys"! Damn if they didnt just show me on the news in the lead and then losing to a honda prelude! ReVenGe will be mine!<P>So Chris, do you have any baffled pans ready to ship? It seems to me that you would have to make it according to your post but never hurts to ask. Hmm wonder if adding approx 1/2 quart would help next time? May create some windage but who knows?<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000005||c m west||06-13-2001||11:53 PM||||at this time we dontg, however - when you find it most convenient for you, just take off you pan and send it to us. Give Chris West a call here at the shop to work out the details<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BV MotorSports||06-14-2001||12:07 AM||||Thanx, will see if I can yank one off of one of the parts cars at my "use to be" buddies shop. Dont want the Fiero to be parked. Just got her back and on the road after setting for 1 yr. Sorry part is, first day IO drove her some morron hit her in the parking lot at work. Sorry a$$ cameras are so cheap we couldnt make out who did it. Minor damage but it pisses me off!<BR>Anyway, back to the subject! Wonder if a windage tray would be worth while while I am at it? Any experience with them? I dont want to get too far into the 2.8 since I am building a 3.8na for the car. Hmm I should drop the oil pan on that one and see if its baffled. I need to drill the pan to add an oil drain for the turbo I am building for the 3.8 anyway.<BR>Be in touch. Thanks!<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||14
Z||000007||Greg Piet||06-14-2001||11:45 AM||||OK I have done the autocrossing and a wee bit of racing on road courses.  What are the turning specs of your cars so that you are starving Oil(at least for the sensor to cut engine) and Fuel?<P>My car has only pulled 1.15 lateral g's on an autocross track, and 1.05 on the road course(it was a school and I was runnign street tires) according to my G-tech.<P>In the autocrosses I have NEVER oil starved my car.  When I was 1 mark above E on the gas gauge I did not lose fuel pressure.  I typically run at autoX events with 1/2 to 1/4 tank so I have enough Fuel to finish the day.<P>Never had any starvation probs on the road course either||||reg||1
Z||000008||BV MotorSports||06-14-2001||11:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Greg Piet:<BR><B>OK I have done the autocrossing and a wee bit of racing on road courses.  What are the turning specs of your cars so that you are starving Oil(at least for the sensor to cut engine) and Fuel?<P>My car has only pulled 1.15 lateral g's on an autocross track, and 1.05 on the road course(it was a school and I was runnign street tires) according to my G-tech.<P>In the autocrosses I have NEVER oil starved my car.  When I was 1 mark above E on the gas gauge I did not lose fuel pressure.  I typically run at autoX events with 1/2 to 1/4 tank so I have enough Fuel to finish the day.<P>Never had any starvation probs on the road course either</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have no clue what lateral G's my hooptie fiero can pull. I dont even have that much suspension work.<BR>ST sway bars frt/rr<BR>ST Lowering springs<BR>Poly everything<BR>RCC bumpsteer (gonna toss this, doesnt work well with lowered car)<BR>Sticky tires.<P>Thats about it for suspension mods. Oil starvation sounds right to me. Gotta baffle the pan!<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000009||c m west||06-14-2001||10:24 PM||||strange, <P> McLaren F1 = .98 G<BR> Testarossa = .95 G<BR> Z06 Corvette = .96 G<P>and you got over 1 lateral g's on you Fiero, impressive to say the least<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||06-14-2001||10:39 PM||||Not really strange. I have been in a few street driven fiero's that will pull over 1 G on street tires. Up until the Z06 , the 84 Z51 held the title for best handling car in North America. <P>I'm sure with my current setup I'm pullin over 1 G on street tires. Just takes tuning. If I recall the Z06 was over 1 lateral G wasn't it??<P>IT's all about tuning , and the fiero to a lot of people is a mystery.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000011||c m west||06-14-2001||10:44 PM||||The Fiero isn't a mystery to me, simply a curse - I have to work on them 14 hours a day<P> just kidding - there not that bad<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||lowCG||06-14-2001||10:49 PM||||I've oil starved in corners,300# springs,sticky street tires,banked offramp.<BR>I heard of someone on this forum using the Accusump system on a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000013||BV MotorSports||06-14-2001||11:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Not really strange. <P>IT's all about tuning , and the fiero to a lot of people is a mystery.<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Jonathan, could you give me a holler of list?<BR>I would like to chat with you about your suspension set-up and those big brakes. We spoke a long time ago so I doubt you would remember me. Anyway e-mail addy below:<P>bv_motorsports@hotmail.com<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||6
Z||000014||Greg Piet||06-15-2001||01:47 AM||||accd to R+T stock Fiero pulls .84 on a skidpad.  My G-tech told me the exact same number when I was running stock suspension on my Yoko's<BR>I have made a skidpad before an autocross (It pays to be the director), and on a true skid pad on my Yoko S306 street tires I pulled 1.01g's after my suspension mods.  The 1.05 was on a road course, so there are hills, slight banks, etc...<BR>The 1.15 was on Hoosier A3S03 autocross tires<P>My suspension isnt that tweaked.<BR>Eibach<BR>KYB<BR>Poly<BR>Rear sway<BR>Stock front sway<BR>Rear at max neg camber<P>I dont even have coil overs yet (Gimmee Time)<P>How do you folks oil starve your cars I dont understand...<P>And Yeah the z06 off the factory line pulls 1.01||||reg||1
Z||000015||BV MotorSports||06-15-2001||11:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Greg Piet:<BR><B>hills, slight banks, etc...<BR>How do you folks oil starve your cars I dont understand...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The key word is "banked" turn. Not flat turn.<BR>I have never had my car shut down to oil pick up bein uncovered during autoX or just hard driving. But add a Banked left turn and nadda...no go!<P>Steven<BR><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||9
Z||000016||ThatRickGuy||06-15-2001||12:34 PM||||hey BV, when you mentioned getting bumped in a parking lot it reminded me of a past topic. Somebody had posted about how there car had gotten 'bumped' similarly and they were having fuel problems, if I remember right his fuel pump had loosened up inside the tank. might be something else to check out.||||reg||1
Z||000017||BV MotorSports||06-15-2001||04:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ThatRickGuy:<BR><B>hey BV, when you mentioned getting bumped in a parking lot it reminded me of a past topic. Somebody had posted about how there car had gotten 'bumped' similarly and they were having fuel problems, if I remember right his fuel pump had loosened up inside the tank. might be something else to check out.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmmm...well the car has ran fine b4 and after the "incident". Minor damage, plastic trim (rounded) on the door and above the ram-air scoop broken, scuffed up the ram-air scoop and scuffed the top of my drivers side mirror. Was quoted $150 to fix.<BR>$150 (minor) fix but UGLY to look at 4 now!<P><BR>Thanks for the info guys.<P>Steven<BR><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
